      "completed_at": "2026-05-06T14:15:23Z",
      "duration_ms": 81000,
      "summary": [
        "Created tools/seed-truncate.php and tools/seed-insert.php as process-isolated CLI seed scripts. Updated composer.json seed-tests script from a single ComposerScripts::seedTests() callback to an array of two php commands. Verified composer seed-tests exits 0 on a live test database. No resetCollection() calls present in either script. The two-process split eliminates the need for ORM cache invalidation between truncation and insertion."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "tools/seed-truncate.php",
          "tools/seed-insert.php",
          "composer.json"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-06T14:15:23Z",
          "note": "vendor/shark/simple_html_dom/simple_html_dom.php (lines 99, 102, 113) uses the deprecated locally-scoped $http_response_header variable. This surfaces as PHP 8.4 deprecation notices on every bootstrap and clutters seed/test output. Out of scope here but should be patched or the package replaced."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-06T14:15:23Z",
          "note": "ComposerScripts::doSeedTests() still contains the now-unused resetCollection() calls and the combined truncate+seed logic. Now that both operations run in separate processes via the CLI scripts, doSeedTests() and seedTests() are dead code paths for the seed-tests workflow. Consider deprecating or removing them to avoid confusion."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-06T14:15:23Z",
          "note": "tools/setup-local.php uses require_once __DIR__ . '/include/cli-utilities.php' for shared CLI helpers, while the new seed scripts require the test bootstrap directly. This is intentional given their different purposes, but a brief comment in each script clarifying why they do not use cli-utilities.php would help future maintainers."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-05-06T14:14:02Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-05-06T14:15:23Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-06T14:15:23Z",
      "notes": [
        "All five acceptance criteria are met and verified by a successful `composer seed-tests` run (exit 0). The two scripts are process-isolated: seed-truncate.php clears all tables, then seed-insert.php seeds users/locales/countries in a fresh process — no ORM cache bleed-over. Pre-existing deprecation notices from vendor/shark/simple_html_dom are unrelated to these changes. QA should verify: (1) each script runs independently with the correct exit code, (2) running seed-tests twice in a row (idempotency via composer) succeeds, (3) no resetCollection() calls appear in the new scripts."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

